Again, listen to David.  At this point, I'd also suggest you play
Lawful.  Not so much because of Excalibur, but just to make it so your
favorite artifacts aren't available so you'll stop passing things up
in order to maximize your chances of getting them.  An arti-wishless
#conduct would actually make things easier for you.

Gehennom is *not hard* for a character who can actually get there. I'm
by no means a serial ascender myself, but my deaths are *always* in
the early to mid game.  Every time I've reached the Castle, I've gone
on to ascend.  And the wand just makes it easier, even if you don't
get a single artifact from it.

Consider these wishes:
2 blessed scrolls of charging
     maximize the wand's use
2 scrolls of genocide
     bless one and take out L. curse one and get SDSM.
blessed fixed +2 speed boots
     5/3 normal speed, plus AC
cloak of magic resistance
     The most fashionable accessory for a suit of SDSM
magic marker
     Have you seen a useful scroll? Do you have a useless scrolls?
     Would you rather it were the other way around? Now it can be.

And still have 1 or 2 wishes left over for a cockatrice corpse
and a wrest final item.  No artifacts on that list, but if I'm
missing any of those things (or their equivalent), I'd probably wish
for it rather than an artifact *even if I stand a good chance of
getting it*. (with the exception of the scrolls, since I prefer to do
genocideless to make Gehennom a bit more challenging.)

So here's what you need to do.  Go into wizard mode.  Wish for:
+4 suit of SDSM, +4 cloak of MR, AoLS. BoH, +4 speed boots,
+4 T-Shirt, +4 gloves of whatever, +4 helmet of whatever, wand of
fire, 2 wands of digging, 2 +5 silver sabers, ring of levitation, ring
of free action, 20 K-rations, enough tins to get all the intrinsics, a
pickaxe, 3 cursed scrolls of teleportation, 20 +5 daggers, 10 blessed
potions of gain ability, and whatever other miscellaneous items you
want...but *no* artifacts at all.  #enhance saber, two-weapon, and
dagger as high as you can. (you can do it without training in
wizmode.)

Then levelport to Gehennom and see how easy it is.  Then consider
that when you do it in a real game, you'll have the Orb of Fate
halving all the damage you take and giving you unlimited levelport,
and a whole lot of other situational items that you happened to find
on your way there.  If you do die, consider what item would have
prevented it: in 9 out of 10 cases, it won't be an artifact.
And as long as you're there, wish for a scroll of create monster
and summon Demogorgon (wizmode lets you specify a monster).  He's
the real challenge, so get some practice fighting him. (I understand
he's not as bad as he was in 3.3.1, though. I haven't seen him
recently.)  If you want, wish up the Bell and do the ascension run
itself, but there are a few more items you'll want to have before you
do that (none of them artifacts).



